        "id": "R1",
        "found": true,
        "by": {
          "claim": "The sync path enforces least-privilege via `destinationServiceAccounts`, but the server-side diff path ignores this control and falls back to the cluster credential, requiring unbounded `patch` RBAC. An attacker who can trigger a diff operation can probe or modify cluster-scoped resources through the diff interface that sync is explicitly designed to block. The credential at risk is the cluster credential's unbounded write authority, and the blast radius extends to every resource kind the cluster credential can patch. The gap is that the diff path's identity check is not enforced at the decision point where the sync identity is scoped.",
          "citations": [
            "rfc-001-sync-impersonation.md",
            "tickets/T-28695.md"
          ]
        }
      },
